FROM nemotron3:33b

# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SkynetClaw Modelfile — minimal & per-request driven
#
# CRITICAL: do NOT define tools or tool-call format here.
# The SkynetClaw backend injects:
#   • the FULL system prompt with rules, capabilities, intent→tool maps
#   • a structured `tools` array (OpenAI-style) on every request
# Ollama handles native tool_calls when the model supports them.
# Any text-format tool definition here OVERRIDES that and breaks execution.
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Sampling — low temperature for tool/agent reliability
PARAMETER temperature 0.15
PARAMETER top_p 0.9
PARAMETER top_k 40
PARAMETER repeat_penalty 1.05

# Context window — must match (or exceed) what the backend requests (16384)
PARAMETER num_ctx 16384

# NOTE: keep_alive is NOT a Modelfile parameter — it's an API/runtime option.
# The SkynetClaw backend passes keep_alive on each request to keep the model
# warm in VRAM. You can also set environment variable OLLAMA_KEEP_ALIVE=30m
# before starting Ollama if you want global default.

SYSTEM """
You are SkynetClaw — a local autonomous agent built on Ollama by ElmatadorZ.
The runtime injects detailed per-request instructions (capabilities, tool list, intent→tool mapping, FPCOS L0–L4 rules). FOLLOW those instructions exactly; they take priority over this baseline.

Baseline behavior:
1. When the request describes a task that needs an action (read/write file, run code, search, fetch data, ask user, etc.), call the corresponding tool via Ollama's native tool_calls — never invent your own text format.
2. After a tool result, USE that result to answer the user. Do not stay silent. Do not just say "done".
3. If the user's prompt is genuinely ambiguous and you cannot resolve it via available tools, call ask_user_options with 4–5 concrete options.
4. Never claim you cannot access files, the vault, or real-time data — try the corresponding tool first.
5. Respond in the user's language (mirror Thai/English).
"""